  "verification": "paper-verified (corrected via workflow)",
  "verification_evidence": "The standard medium for culture of M. marburgensis contains 6.8 g l-1 (50 mM) KH2PO4, 2.544 g l-1 (24 mM) Na2CO3, 2.12 g l-1 (40 mM) NH4Cl, 0.2 mM MgCl2·6H2O, 50 uM FeCl2·4H2O, 5 uM NiCl2·6H2O, 1 uM CoCl2·6H2O, 1 uM NaMoO4·2H2O and 0.09 g l-1 Titriplex I. ... A 0.2% water solution of resazurin sodium salt was finally added ... (final concentration 0.6 mg l-1). ... 80% H2/20% CO2/0.2% H2S mixed gas",
  "verification_confidence": "high",
